<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::international_support_fl" target="iran_maritime_pressure::maritime_security_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained increases in Western military and materiel support to Ukraine divert naval assets, patrol rotations, and ISR resources away from the Middle East, reducing aggregate maritime security presence and interdiction capacity in key sea lanes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_maritime_pressure</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::international_support_fl" target="treasury_market_stress::debt_issuance_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Large, sustained external military and fiscal assistance programs trigger supplemental appropriations and financing decisions that increase scheduled sovereign debt issuance to cover support costs.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">treasury_market_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::international_support_fl" target="us_canada_tariff_row::political_pressure_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Large, visible increases in US/Canadian military and financial support for Ukraine generate domestic scrutiny and constituency demands to prioritize or protect local industries, raising pressure on leaders to take tariff or trade-positioning actions in the bilateral dispute.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_canada_tariff_row</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::international_support_fl" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained large-scale military and economic assistance programs mobilize public procurement and signal elevated geopolitical risk, prompting private and public investors to direct additional capital toward defense- and dual-use AI platforms and infrastructure in US/allied markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
