  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A noticeable drop in perceived fiscal credibility weakens other actors' belief in the durability and political will behind US sanctions, leading banks and traders to lower voluntary compliance and increase tolerance for secondary exposure to Iranian counterparties.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">treasury_market_stress</data>
